  "description": "\u201cThe point of concurrence of the three perimeter-bisecting splitters joining vertices A, B, C to the excircle touchpoints.\u201d\n\u2014 Clark Kimberling's Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers (ETC) \u2022 X_8 (Nagel Point)\n\nInteractive GEOMETOR Explorer page: https://geometor.github.io/etc/centers/c-00001-00019/x-00008/\n\n1 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: X_8 = Nagel Point \u2022 [A N_a] \u2229 [B N_b] \u2229 [C N_c]\n2 \u00b7 GOAL: X_8 = Nagel Point \u2022 [A N_a] \u2229 [B N_b] \u2229 [C N_c]\n3 \u00b7 ASSERT: Trilinears (s-a)/a : (s-b)/b : (s-c)/c \u2022 Barycentrics s-a : s-b : s-c\n4 \u00b7 INTERSECT: Nagel Line {1, 2, 8, 10} \u2022 Fuhrmann Line {4, 8} \u2022 Line {7, 8}\n5 \u00b7 INTERSECT: Nagel Line {1, 2, 8, 10} \u2022 Fuhrmann Line {4, 8} \u2022 Line {7, 8}\n6 \u00b7 PROVE: Anticomplement of X_1 \u2022 Isotomic Conjugate X_7 \u2022 Isogonal X_56\n7 \u00b7 \u2234: Kimberling (6, 9, 13) Search = 4.507489358552\n\nGEOMETOR \u2022 ETC \u2022 X_8",
